{"kind":"charness.bounded_review.v1","lens":"bounded fresh-eye causal reviewer; Fresh-Eye Satisfaction: parent-delegated","packet_sha256":"94a9dbfd918e2bb4d7f180a2bc11585cd17d49787afa2751b9b741a3b7783ec2","reviewed_input_identity_sha256":"65c7e5db9265d28776a9e0c01d0281b3452afb6bdd51291b47107dcf46e915b0","verdict":"pass","target_observations":[{"target":"https://github.com/corca-ai/charness/issues/813","verdict":"pass","summary":"The supplied substrate supports the pre-design causal classification and bounded sibling scope; implementation and live hard-kill proof remain explicitly open.","evidence":["charness-artifacts/debug/2026-09-12-issue-813-temp-output-ownership.md:49","charness-artifacts/debug/2026-09-12-issue-813-temp-output-ownership.md:102"]}],"findings":[{"id":"JTBD","severity":"information","summary":"Every Charness temporary-output producer must have an attributable lifecycle so success, failure, timeout, cancellation, inspection, and GC cannot leave or delete unknown state.","evidence":["charness-artifacts/debug/2026-09-12-issue-813-temp-output-ownership.md:10"],"action":"Use this invariant as the design boundary."},{"id":"classification-confirmation","severity":"information","summary":"Confirmed as a repeated-symptom ownership-seam defect, not a defect in the existing owned-scratch primitive.","evidence":["charness-artifacts/debug/2026-09-12-issue-813-temp-output-ownership.md:35","charness-artifacts/debug/2026-09-12-issue-813-temp-output-ownership.md:102","tests/test_runtime_scratch.py:111"],"action":"Retain the stated classification."},{"id":"root-cause","severity":"high","summary":"Disconfirmer-first: focused lifecycle, refusal, promotion, and recovery evidence contradicts primitive failure. Five whys converge on local temp selection → caller-local cleanup → normal-exit tests appear sufficient → adoption remains voluntary → no mandatory classification boundary connects producers to inspection/GC.","evidence":["charness-artifacts/debug/2026-09-12-issue-813-temp-output-ownership.md:35","charness-artifacts/debug/2026-09-12-issue-813-temp-output-ownership.md:54","scripts/agent-runtime/run-local-eval-test.mjs:77"],"action":"Carry this causal chain into design without treating local cleanup as ownership proof."},{"id":"debug-artifact","severity":"information","summary":"The artifact is adequate for pre-design use: it separates observed facts, disconfirmed cause, falsifiable hypothesis, invariant, seam risk, and non-claims. Implementation verification is correctly pending.","evidence":["charness-artifacts/debug/2026-09-12-issue-813-temp-output-ownership.md:16","charness-artifacts/debug/2026-09-12-issue-813-temp-output-ownership.md:42","charness-artifacts/debug/2026-09-12-issue-813-temp-output-ownership.md:49"],"action":"Preserve it as the causal substrate."},{"id":"invariant-proof","severity":"high","summary":"Producer-to-final-consumer proof holds: shell and JS sites create system-temp directories with local cleanup, while the registry enumerates only <runtime-root>/scratch/<producer>/<run>. Therefore those producers cannot be attributed, inspected, recovered, or safely GC-classified by the final consumer after abrupt loss.","evidence":["scripts/check-shell.sh:39","scripts/check-python-lint.sh:67","scripts/check-links-internal.sh:70","scripts/check-markdown.sh:91","scripts/check-secrets.sh:125","scripts/agent-runtime/run-local-eval-test.mjs:77","charness-artifacts/debug/2026-09-12-issue-813-temp-output-ownership.md:62","scripts/runtime_scratch_registry.py:129"],"action":"Treat registry visibility as the proof obligation."},{"id":"detection-gap","severity":"high","summary":"Current tests establish owned-root behavior but do not sample every producer class, and no production gate rejects missing or stale producer classification. Green normal-exit tests therefore cannot detect anonymous roots left by cancellation or host loss.","evidence":["charness-artifacts/debug/2026-09-12-issue-813-temp-output-ownership.md:77","tests/test_runtime_scratch.py:28","tests/test_runtime_scratch_failures.py:330"],"action":"Keep the detection gap open until negative controls and terminal-path evidence exist."},{"id":"sibling-search","severity":"high","summary":"Four-axis search is coherent: same layer—shell checks plus Claude evaluator; abstraction up—all production temp creators; specialization down—atomic sibling files and anonymous auto-delete handles are outside this directory-leak class; cross-file—the registry cannot infer external roots. Python directory constructors were searched behaviorally but no unresolved instance is evidenced here.","evidence":["charness-artifacts/debug/2026-09-12-issue-813-temp-output-ownership.md:86","charness-artifacts/debug/2026-09-12-issue-813-temp-output-ownership.md:92","charness-artifacts/debug/2026-09-12-issue-813-temp-output-ownership.md:98"],"action":"Bundle the evidenced directory-producing siblings; defer unsampled external-tool hard-kill behavior and unobserved constructor families."},{"id":"bundle-vs-defer","severity":"information","summary":"Recommendation: bundle the seven evidenced anonymous directory producers because they share one causal seam and failure mode. Defer atomic files, anonymous auto-delete handles, pre-existing /tmp debris, and unsampled external-tool hard-kill claims.","evidence":["charness-artifacts/debug/2026-09-12-issue-813-temp-output-ownership.md:23","charness-artifacts/debug/2026-09-12-issue-813-temp-output-ownership.md:73","charness-artifacts/debug/2026-09-12-issue-813-temp-output-ownership.md:110"],"action":"Keep bundle and defer boundaries explicit in the design record."}],"counterweight_triage":[{"concern":"Root-cause over-reach","bin":"bounded","disposition":"Does not blame the primitive; passing focused tests disconfirm that candidate, while adoption remains the evidenced cause."},{"concern":"Detection-gap over-reach","bin":"bounded","disposition":"Claims absence of a producer-classification gate, not absence of all lifecycle testing."},{"concern":"Sibling-search over-reach","bin":"bounded","disposition":"Bundles only evidenced directory producers; atomic files, anonymous handles, existing debris, and unsampled hard-kill behavior remain outside the claim."}],"next_move":"Proceed to specification with the causal classification intact; do not treat this review as implementation approval or live-behavior proof.","non_claims":["No implementation design or fix is prescribed.","No workspace state was consulted beyond the inline semantic payload.","No claim is made that every external tool survives or cleans up after host hard-kill.","Goal evidence lineage is not-goal-bound: binding, draft, goal_run, and work_item are null.","Fresh-Eye Satisfaction: parent-delegated."]}
